WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.818 --> 00:00:10.179
Cleo trudged into the kitchen after school.

2
00:00:10.199 --> 00:00:12.179
"What's wrong?"

3
00:00:12.459 --> 00:00:13.100
Mom asked.

4
00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:16.181
"Everyone is playing BattleQuest.

5
00:00:17.501 --> 00:00:22.082
It's a new online game, and it's the only thing Rea and Noah ever talk about."

6
00:00:23.083 --> 00:00:23.863
Cleo sighed.

7
00:00:23.883 --> 00:00:27.284
"I'm tired of being left out of the fun."

8
00:00:28.404 --> 00:00:33.087
"Well, once you save enough allowance, you can join the fun," Mom said.

9
00:00:34.288 --> 00:00:35.108
Cleo sighed.

10
00:00:36.769 --> 00:00:40.071
She went into the living room and plopped in front of the family computer.

11
00:00:41.212 --> 00:00:45.655
If she couldn't play BattleQuest herself, she'd have to settle for watching other people play.

12
00:00:47.136 --> 00:00:50.578
She'd just finished watching a video when an ad flashed on the screen.

13
00:00:51.879 --> 00:00:53.400
Cleo couldn't believe her luck!

14
00:00:54.688 --> 00:00:57.310
"Free One-Day Trial of BattleQuest!"

15
00:00:57.731 --> 00:00:58.251
she read.

16
00:00:59.812 --> 00:01:04.376
She clicked the link and entered a username, her email, and her favorite password.

17
00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:11.482
As the game downloaded, she had a sudden thought.

18
00:01:11.502 --> 00:01:14.184
"I should've asked Mom's permission.

19
00:01:15.185 --> 00:01:16.086
But it is free.

20
00:01:16.506 --> 00:01:17.307
It'll be fine."

21
00:01:18.768 --> 00:01:23.712
When Cleo entered the world of BattleQuest, it somehow looked different from the videos.

22
00:01:25.644 --> 00:01:28.386
"This must be the latest version," she reasoned.

23
00:01:29.367 --> 00:01:33.009
She tried searching for her friends' IDs but couldn't find them.

24
00:01:34.270 --> 00:01:38.253
It didn't really matter though—Cleo was finally playing BattleQuest!

25
00:01:40.154 --> 00:01:44.517
The next morning Cleo met Rea and Noah in the corridor at school.

26
00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:47.319
"BattleQuest is so much fun!"

27
00:01:47.699 --> 00:01:48.460
she exclaimed.

28
00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:51.922
"You didn't tell me there were dragons in the game!"

29
00:01:53.123 --> 00:01:54.644
Rea and Noah looked at each other.

30
00:01:55.712 --> 00:01:57.913
"Dragons?" Noah asked.

31
00:01:57.933 --> 00:02:02.215
"I wish my free trial lasted longer than one day."

32
00:02:04.436 --> 00:02:05.196
Cleo sighed.

33
00:02:05.216 --> 00:02:10.158
"What are you talking about Rea began when Cleo's phone chirped.

34
00:02:11.499 --> 00:02:14.420
Cleo checked her phone and saw a text from her cousin.

35
00:02:15.461 --> 00:02:16.821
Just got a weird email from you.

36
00:02:17.101 --> 00:02:22.464
Spam? "That's strange," Cleo said when her phone chirped again.

37
00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:26.641
A friend from camp texted to say she got a similar email.

38
00:02:28.002 --> 00:02:31.744
Moments later Cleo's tennis coach also texted about spam.

39
00:02:31.764 --> 00:02:35.285
"It sounds like you got hacked," Noah said.

40
00:02:36.706 --> 00:02:41.668
Cleo wasn't looking forward to telling Mom about the spam emails, but it turned out she didn't have

41
00:02:41.728 --> 00:02:47.310
to. When she got home, Mom and Uncle Roger were hunched over the family computer.

42
00:02:47.330 --> 00:02:50.932
"Then the screen went black," Mom explained.

43
00:02:51.820 --> 00:02:55.903
"A window popped up saying if I wanted my data, I'd have to pay a ransom.

44
00:02:57.224 --> 00:02:58.825
I couldn't—even if I wanted to!

45
00:02:59.906 --> 00:03:03.829
The bank put a hold on my account today after several suspicious charges."

46
00:03:03.849 --> 00:03:06.791
"You got infected by ransomware.

47
00:03:07.731 --> 00:03:10.033
Good thing there's a security specialist in the family."

48
00:03:11.054 --> 00:03:12.275
Uncle Roger smiled.

49
00:03:12.295 --> 00:03:15.417
"Have either of you downloaded anything recently?"

50
00:03:15.437 --> 00:03:18.439
"I haven't," Mom said.

51
00:03:18.459 --> 00:03:22.917
"Cleo?" Cleo's cheeks turned red.

52
00:03:22.937 --> 00:03:27.540
"Does a free trial of BattleQuest count?"

53
00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:31.343
"Absolutely," Uncle Roger said.

54
00:03:31.363 --> 00:03:36.727
"Hackers use links like that to trick people into installing malware on their computers.

55
00:03:37.827 --> 00:03:43.211
Then they take control of your computer and steal your personal information like passwords and banking information."

56
00:03:44.172 --> 00:03:45.252
Cleo looked at Mom.

57
00:03:45.272 --> 00:03:52.262
"Sorry. BattleQuest is the only thing my friends talk about, and I was tired of feeling left out."

58
00:03:52.282 --> 00:03:56.626
"I'm glad you told us," Uncle Roger said.

59
00:03:56.646 --> 00:03:59.369
"It will make it easier to fix the problem.

60
00:04:00.369 --> 00:04:04.834
Anyone can be a victim of identity theft, but there are steps people can take to be safer.

61
00:04:05.955 --> 00:04:10.299
To start, I'll install antivirus software to keep you safe from viruses and ransomware.

62
00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:12.701
I'll also set up a firewall."

63
00:04:13.522 --> 00:04:14.563
"What's a firewall?"

64
00:04:14.803 --> 00:04:15.504
Cleo asked.

65
00:04:17.204 --> 00:04:22.266
"It's a program that filters information coming from the internet into your computer," Uncle Roger explained.

66
00:04:22.286 --> 00:04:25.988
"It's like a window screen that keeps bugs out.

67
00:04:27.249 --> 00:04:31.470
But in order for a firewall to work, you have to scan your computer on a regular basis."

68
00:04:35.092 --> 00:04:36.853
there anything else we should do differently?"

69
00:04:37.233 --> 00:04:39.414
Mom asked, giving Cleo a stern look.

70
00:04:40.694 --> 00:04:43.956
"Never reuse passwords," Uncle Roger said.

71
00:04:44.992 --> 00:04:49.340
"Watch out for links with misspellings and ads or pop-ups promising something for nothing."

72
00:04:50.763 --> 00:04:53.047
"I've learned that the hard way," Cleo said.

73
00:04:53.067 --> 00:04:56.694
"'Free' doesn't always mean free from trouble!"
